meta {
  name: Where content sits in the syllabus
  seq: 11
}

docs {
  A placement is the join between folder 10's two halves: this book, these
  pages, that syllabus point. It is what turns "search the library" into
  "answer this question from what the class is actually being taught", and it
  is the only place page ranges are recorded.

  Placements are proposed, then confirmed or rejected. Machine suggestions and
  a teacher's own mapping arrive on the same route and are told apart by
  origin, so nothing an extraction pipeline guessed is used to answer a pupil
  until a person has agreed with it.

  Everything here is deleted again before folder 12, because a curriculum node
  with a placement on it cannot be removed.
}
